          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>After caring for a patient on contact precautions, you begin removing (doffing) </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>After caring for a patient on contact precautions, you begin removing (doffing) your PPE. Which component should be removed FIRST?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gloves</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct! Gloves are the most contaminated PPE component (direct patient/environment contact). Removing them first — followed immediately by hand hygiene — prevents transferring pathogens to other PPE during subsequent removal steps.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gown</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The gown is removed after gloves and hand hygiene. If you remove the gown first while still wearing contaminated gloves, you risk spreading organisms from glove surfaces to your skin and clothing beneath.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mask or respirator</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The mask/respirator is removed last (or second-to-last before final hand hygiene). It continues to protect your respiratory tract from any organisms aerosolised during removal of other items.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Eye protection</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Eye protection is removed after the gown but before the mask. The correct doffing sequence is: Gloves → Hand hygiene → Gown → Eye protection → Mask/respirator → Final hand hygiene.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Remember the doffing sequence: Gloves (most contaminated) → Hand hygiene → Gown → Eye protection → Mask (protects airway longest) → Final hand hygiene. The principle is to remove the most contaminated items first while keeping respiratory protection until last."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done — removing the most contaminated item first and performing hand hygiene immediately prevents self-contamination during the rest of the doffing sequence."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
